A ball released at the top of long ramp inclined at an angle $\theta = 30.0^\circ$ to the horizontal roles down the ramp with negligible friction. If the length of the ramp is $8.00\ \mathrm{m}$ and the mass of the ball is $0.500\ \mathrm{kg}$, calculate:

(i) its acceleration down the ramp;

(ii) the time it takes to the reach the base of the ramp;

(iii) The friction on the floor after the ramp which brings the ball to rest $15.0\ \mathrm{m}$ from the base of the ramp. *[4 marks]*
